  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G2M">Definition <span data-tag="0G2M">101.24.1</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. We say $f$ is <em>quasi-finite</em> if $f$ is locally quasi-finite (Definition <a href="/tag/06PU" data-tag="06PU">101.23.2</a>) and quasi-compact (Definition <a href="/tag/050U" data-tag="050U">101.7.2</a>). </p>
